# Google Identity Services web client id. This is public configuration: it is
# bundled into the browser by Vite and is safe to expose. Copy this file to
# `.env.local`, which Vite reads and which is ignored by Git.
#
# It must be the same value as GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID in backend/.env.
#
# The backend is always the authority. It decides whether Google sign-in is
# available, issues the single-use nonce, and rejects any credential whose
# audience is not its own GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID. Setting this variable alone does
# NOT enable sign-in: if the backend has no client id, the sign-in card shows an
# unavailable notice and only password sign-in works. Leave it unset to simply
# take the client id from GET /api/auth/google/config/ instead.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=

# Exact origins. The client id is only accepted by Google when the browser origin
# matches an authorized JavaScript origin on the OAuth client EXACTLY (scheme,
# host and port; no trailing slash). Use your own values here:
#
#   Development : http://localhost:5173
#                 http://127.0.0.1:5173
#   Production  : https://attendance.youruniversity.edu
#
# `http://localhost:5173` and `http://127.0.0.1:5173` are different origins, so
# both must be listed if you use both. The same values belong in
# TRUSTED_ORIGINS in backend/.env.

# Optional. Overrides where the development API is proxied from.
# VITE_API_PROXY_TARGET=http://127.0.0.1:8000
